# AUTHOR-PAREN PRESERVATION — the COSTUME axis: one cell per syntactic position
# where a grouping paren can sit, so a partial fix fingers exactly what it
# missed. Every paren below is REDUNDANT (the compiler parses the same program
# without it) and every one of them survives `gg fmt`.
#
# Cells, and what each samples:
#   * `(not x) and y` ......... a PREFIX-operator operand (`format_prefix_operand`)
#   * `(*b) + 1` .............. a deref operand — the second prefix costume
#   * `(a).len()` ............. a single-identifier POSTFIX RECEIVER. Not the
#                               same cell as `(a + b).m()`: that pair is REQUIRED
#                               by `needs_parens_as_postfix_receiver` and comes
#                               back on every build, so it would be green for a
#                               reason unrelated to preservation.
#   * `(slen as bool)` ........ a cast in CONDITION position
#   * `n + (n * shift)` ....... a whole arithmetic sub-term as an infix operand
#   * `(((x)))` ............... the DEPTH cell: three layers, pinning that the
#                               layer count is the push multiplicity and not a
#                               boolean
#   * `f"{(a + b) * c}"` ...... an f-string INTERIOR — a POS PIN, see below.
#
# RED (pre-fix binary, this fixture): `not x and y`, `*b + 1`, `a.len()`,
# `if slen as bool:`, `n + n * shift`, `x` — every cell but the f-string one.
#
# ⚠ The f-string cell has NO constructible red, and the header says so rather
# than implying coverage it does not have. Interpolation bodies never reach the
# paren table at all (a SEPARATE `Parser` parses them and its table is
# discarded, and its synthetic span space is disjoint from any real offset), and
# they are re-emitted from the literal's own segment text. Break-and-watch,
# measured on this tree: forcing `string_literal_text` to `None` — the verbatim
# recovery this cell was thought to rest on — leaves `f"{(a + b) * c}"`
# UNCHANGED, while it reds seven `fmt_form_string_*` tests that guard the
# escape/quote/multiline forms. What this cell pins, then, is that
# interpolation interiors stay out of the paren mechanism: it goes red if
# preservation ever starts rewriting inside a literal.

bool flag(bool x, bool y):
    return (not x) and y

int deref_cell(Box[int] b):
    return (*b) + 1

int recv_cell(String a):
    return (a).len()

int cast_cell(int slen):
    if (slen as bool):
        return 1
    return 0

int scaled(int n, int shift):
    return n + (n * shift)

int depth3(int x):
    return (((x)))

int interp(int a, int b, int c):
    String s = f"{(a + b) * c}"
    return s.len()

void main():
    print(flag(false, true))
    print(deref_cell(Box(1)))
    print(recv_cell("seven"))
    print(cast_cell(2))
    print(scaled(3, 4))
    print(depth3(9))
    print(interp(1, 2, 3))
